{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "GWDOOrographicStatistics",
    "description": "What the sub-grid orography looks like TO THE LOW-LEVEL WIND, and the wave stress it launches. Lines 343-377 and 461-494 of `phys/physics_mmm/bl_gwdo.F90` (WRF 4.8, NCAR/MMM-physics CCPP kernel `bl_gwdo_run`).\n\nWPS supplies the sub-grid orography as EIGHT direction-resolved numbers per grid cell -- the asymmetry oa1..oa4 and the along-ridge length fraction ol1..ol4, each on the four axes W-E, S-N, SW-NE and NW-SE -- plus the standard deviation var, the convexity oc1 and the maximum height ELVMAX. GWDO reduces that to a single along-wind pair by rounding the direction of the low-level mean wind onto an eight-sector rose and reading the statistics of the matching axis, with a sign flip on the asymmetry for the four sectors that point the other way along an axis. It then takes the CROSS-wind length fraction from the perpendicular axis, and their ratio od is the horizontal aspect ratio of the obstacle as the flow meets it. Everything else follows: the obstacle's effective wavenumber coefm = (1 + ol)^(oa + 1) divided by the effective grid length, the Froude number Fr = N var od / U, the asymmetry enhancement (oa + 2)^(ce Fr), the convexity factor Fr^2 oc / (Fr^2 oc + cg), and finally the launch stress taub.\n\nGUARDS. The Fortran computes the launch block only inside `if (.not. ldrag)`, and leaves fr, efac, gfac, coefm and xlinv undefined otherwise -- which is why the diagnostic build had to be changed to read them inside that branch rather than wholesale. Here the branch is arithmetic instead: `on = 1 - ldrag` multiplies every launched quantity, and the two inputs that could be non-finite in an off column (a non-positive low-level N^2, whose square root is taken, and a zero orographic standard deviation, which would put a 1/Fr in the non-hydrostatic factor at infinity) are replaced by unit stand-ins there. A stand-in never reaches an answer: every quantity built from one is multiplied by `on`. The two PURELY orographic quantities, coefm and xlinv, are left unguarded, because the obstacle's length scale exists whether or not the flow is drag-producing; the Fortran simply never asks for it.\n\nThe non-hydrostatic correction of Xu et al. (2024) is optional in WRF (`if_nonhyd`) and is ON in the reference run. It is carried here as a 0/1 parameter multiplying the correction rather than as a branch.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "wrf",
      "gravity-wave-drag",
      "gwdo",
      "orography",
      "wave-launch",
      "column"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Hong, S.-Y., and co-authors (2025). Revision of the orographic gravity wave drag parameterization in the KIAPS Integrated Model. Wea. Forecasting."
      },
      {
        "citation": "Choi, H.-J., and S.-Y. Hong (2015). An updated subgrid orographic parameterization for global atmospheric forecast models. J. Geophys. Res. Atmos. 120, 12445-12457.",
        "doi": "10.1002/2015JD024230"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Kim, Y.-J., and A. Arakawa (1995). Improvement of orographic gravity wave parameterization using a mesoscale gravity wave model. J. Atmos. Sci. 52, 1875-1902.",
        "doi": "10.1175/1520-0469(1995)052<1875:IOOGWP>2.0.CO;2"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Xu, X., and co-authors (2024). Nonhydrostatic effects on orographic gravity wave drag. J. Atmos. Sci.",
        "doi": "10.1175/JAS-D-23-0139.1"
      },
      {
        "citation": "NCAR/MMM-physics bl_gwdo.F90 at commit 52cfbd7 (WRF 4.8 phys/physics_mmm submodule)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "NLEV": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 50,
      "description": "Number of model layers (WRF kte). This component owns no column field of its own; NLEV exists to be bound at the mount edge and passed down to the `col` subsystem, so that an assembly of a different depth does not leave the leaf at its default size."
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "GWDOOrographicStatistics": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "./gwdo_templates.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLEV": "NLEV"
          }
        }
      ],
      "subsystems": {
        "wrf": {
          "ref": "../../../lib/wrf_constants.esm"
        },
        "par": {
          "ref": "./gwdo_parameters.esm"
        },
        "col": {
          "ref": "./column_state.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLEV": "NLEV"
          }
        }
      },
      "variables": {
        "oa1": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Sub-grid orographic asymmetry on the W-E axis (WPS `OA1`)."
        },
        "oa2": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Sub-grid orographic asymmetry on the S-N axis (WPS `OA2`)."
        },
        "oa3": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Sub-grid orographic asymmetry on the SW-NE axis (WPS `OA3`)."
        },
        "oa4": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Sub-grid orographic asymmetry on the NW-SE axis (WPS `OA4`)."
        },
        "ol1": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Fraction of the grid cell occupied by sub-grid ridges on the W-E axis (WPS `OL1`)."
        },
        "ol2": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Same on the S-N axis (WPS `OL2`)."
        },
        "ol3": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Same on the SW-NE axis (WPS `OL3`)."
        },
        "ol4": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Same on the NW-SE axis (WPS `OL4`)."
        },
        "oc1": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Sub-grid orographic convexity (WPS `CON`), the fourth moment of the sub-grid terrain over the square of its variance."
        },
        "dxmeter": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Grid spacing. GWDO sets both the x and the y grid length to this one number, so the along- and cross-wind grid lengths differ only through which of the four rose axes is picked."
        },
        "dx_factor": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Effective-grid-length multiplier for the wave-launch stress (WRF namelist `dx_factor`, default 2)."
        },
        "if_nonhyd": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "1 when the non-hydrostatic correction of Xu et al. (2024) is applied to the launch stress, 0 otherwise (WRF namelist `if_nonhyd`, a logical there). The reference run has it on."
        },
        "on": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "1 when this column produces drag and 0 when the ldrag gate has switched the scheme off; the arithmetic form of the Fortran's `if (.not. ldrag)` guard."
        },
        "wdir": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Direction of the low-level mean wind as an angle in [0, 2 pi], atan2(ubar, vbar) + pi. Carried dimensionless because the only thing done with it is to scale it by mdir/(2 pi) and round the result to an integer sector; pi here is `wrf.piconst`, not the truncated literal WRF passes in (FORTRAN_BUGS N102), which can change the answer only for a wind within 3e-8 of a sector boundary."
        },
        "fdir": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Sectors per radian, mdir/(2 pi)."
        },
        "isec": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Rose sector index in 1..mdir: `mod(nint(fdir wdir), mdir) + 1`. The rounding is written as floor(x + 1/2), which is Fortran's `nint` for the non-negative argument this always has."
        },
        "nwd": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Wind-direction code in 1..8 from the scheme's `nwdir` table (6,7,5,8,2,3,1,4), which maps the rose sector onto the numbering W=1, S=2, SW=3, NW=4, E=5, N=6, NE=7, SE=8."
        },
        "jax": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Orographic AXIS index in 1..4 selected by the wind direction, `mod(nwd-1,4)+1`: the two opposite directions of one axis share the same statistics."
        },
        "jper": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "The axis PERPENDICULAR to jax, the Fortran's `ol4p` permutation (1<->2, 3<->4)."
        },
        "sgn": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "+1 for the four directions with nwd <= 4 and -1 for the other four, the Fortran's `1 - 2 int((nwd-1)/4)`: the asymmetry reverses sign when the wind blows the other way along the same axis."
        },
        "oa": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Sub-grid orographic asymmetry along the low-level wind, signed."
        },
        "ol": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Ridge length fraction along the low-level wind, floored at olmin."
        },
        "olp": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Ridge length fraction across the low-level wind, floored at olmin."
        },
        "oc": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Orographic convexity clamped into [oc_min, oc_max]."
        },
        "od": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Horizontal orographic aspect ratio olp/ol clamped into [odmin, odmax]: how much wider than long the obstacle is as the flow meets it. It scales the Froude number and sets the flow-blocking drag coefficient."
        },
        "dxy": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Grid length along the wind direction: dx on the two cardinal axes and the diagonal sqrt(dx^2 + dy^2) on the two diagonal ones."
        },
        "dxyp": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Grid length across the wind direction, the same table read on the perpendicular axis. With GWDO's dx = dy it equals dxy in every sector; it is written out because the scheme's table would distinguish them on an anisotropic grid."
        },
        "area": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m^2",
          "description": "Grid-cell area dx dy."
        },
        "dx_eff": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Effective grid length for the launch stress, dx_factor (dx + dy)/2."
        },
        "coefm": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Obstacle shape coefficient (1 + ol)^(oa + 1) of Kim and Arakawa (1995): the enhancement of the effective wavenumber by a long, asymmetric ridge. Left UNGUARDED by the ldrag switch, unlike the launched quantities below, because it is a property of the terrain and the wind direction alone; the Fortran computes it inside the guard only because that is the only place it is read."
        },
        "xlinv": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/m",
          "description": "Effective horizontal wavenumber coefm / dx_eff."
        },
        "bnv2_ref": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/s^2",
          "description": "Low-level mean N^2 as the launch block sees it, with a unit stand-in substituted where the column produces no drag. The substitution exists only so that the square root below is real; every quantity built from it is multiplied by `on`."
        },
        "var_ref": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Sub-grid standard deviation as the launch block sees it, with a unit stand-in where the column produces no drag -- otherwise a column switched off BY a zero standard deviation would put a 1/Fr at infinity inside the non-hydrostatic correction."
        },
        "bnv": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/s",
          "description": "Brunt-Vaisala frequency of the launch layer, sqrt(bnv2_ref)."
        },
        "fr": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Froude number of the obstacle, N var od / U, capped at frmax and zeroed where there is no drag. It measures how far the flow must rise over the sub-grid terrain against its own stratification."
        },
        "efac": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Asymmetry enhancement factor (oa + 2)^(ce Fr / frc), clamped into [efacmin, efacmax] and zeroed where there is no drag."
        },
        "gfac": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Convexity factor Fr^2 oc / (Fr^2 oc + cg), which saturates at 1 for a sharp, high obstacle and vanishes for a smooth low one."
        },
        "nhd": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Non-hydrostatic correction of Xu et al. (2024): -9/8 Fr^2 + exp(-2/Fr) (-5/(4 Fr^2) - 1/(2 Fr) + 5/4 + 9 Fr/4 + 9 Fr^2/8). It multiplies the hydrostatic launch stress by (1 + nhd) and is NEGATIVE at the Froude numbers of the reference run (-0.005 to -0.25), i.e. it weakens the drag."
        },
        "taub_hyd": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "Pa",
          "description": "Hydrostatic launch stress rhobar efac xlinv gfac U^3 / N, before the non-hydrostatic correction and before the off switch."
        },
        "taub": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "Pa",
          "description": "Launch (base-level) wave stress: the value the stress profile carries from the surface up to the reference level. Zero wherever ldrag has switched the column off."
        },
        "xn": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Zonal component of the unit vector along the low-level mean wind; the drag is anti-parallel to it. Zero where there is no drag."
        },
        "yn": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Meridional component of the same unit vector."
        },
        "fr_ref": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Froude number built from the stand-ins, so it is strictly positive in EVERY column: bnv is at least 1/s by the stand-in, var_ref at least 1 m, od at least odmin and ulow at least velmin. That matters because the non-hydrostatic correction contains exp(-2/Fr) times -5/(4 Fr^2), which is 0 x (-inf) = NaN at Fr = 0 -- so the off switch cannot be applied to Fr itself and must instead multiply the quantities Fr feeds."
        },
        "efac_ref": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Asymmetry enhancement factor before the off switch."
        },
        "gfac_ref": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Convexity factor before the off switch."
        },
        "nhd_ref": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Non-hydrostatic correction before the off switch."
        },
        "taub_hyd_ref": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "Pa",
          "description": "Hydrostatic launch stress before the off switch."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
